 "Site Type": [
  "Research Station"
 ],
 "Site Name": "Professor Julio Escudero Station",
 "Web Links": [
  "https://www.inach.cl/expedicion-antartica/bases-chilenas-en-antartica-2/base-profesor-julio-escudero/",
  "https://interact-gis.org/Home/Station/109"
 ],
 "Site IDs": [
  "Julio Escudero",
  109
 ],
 "Site Description": "<p>Professor Julio Escudero station is located on Fildes Peninsula, King George Island, Antarctic Specially Protected Area (ASPA) 125. Stations in the nearby area are Bellingshausen (Russia), Artigas (Uruguay), Great Wall Station (China), King Sejong (Korea) and Carlini (Argentina). Othere Chilean facility in the area are Collins, Fildes, Frei and Ripamonti.</p><p>During 1975, some containers were installed to support scientific studies being carried out in the area. The place was known as Refugio Fildes or Fildes station. It was expanded after 1990 with new modules. In 1994, the architecture works began for the first habitational module that was officially opened on February 5, 1995, with a ceremony led by the Director of INACH, Ambassador Oscar Pinochet de la Barra, and attended by several Chilean authorities.\r\nCurrently, the facility has the capacity to accommodate sixty people,\r\na multipurpose laboratory, a laboratory of microbiology and basic\r\nmolecular biology, a wet lab, cold storage rooms and a divers\r\nworking zone</p><p>Atmospheric, biological, environmental, palaeontology, geological research, geomorphology and glaciology studies are conducted at and near the station.</p>",
 "Metadata Updated": "2025-08-27T10:17:34+00:00",
 "Contact Name": [
  "Andrés López"
 ],
 "Organization": [
  "Chilean Antarctic Program"
 ],
 "Elevation": 10,
 "Coordinates": "POINT (301.0378 -62.2014)",
 "Networks": [
  "Polarin"
 ],
 "Operating Status": "Open",
 "Start Year": 1995
}
